From: Fanasina RANDRIATSARAFARA <m.randriatsarafara.f@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:15:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8475-xiaomi-diting: Keep L1C on for the
 fingerprint sensor

The Goodix under-display fingerprint sensor is supplied by L1C (1.8 V)
and L3C (3.3 V) and driven by the secure world over an SPI bus Linux
does not see, so no Linux driver ever votes for L1C. Keep it on.

The sensor reset (TLMM 41) is left to user space, which has to pulse it
the way the vendor HAL does.
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-diting.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-diting.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-diting.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-diting.dts
@@ -528,11 +528,20 @@
 			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_AUTO>;
 		};
 
+		/*
+		 * Also the Goodix fingerprint sensor supply (vendor
+		 * fingerprint_goodix: L1C and L3C). The sensor is driven by
+		 * the secure world over its own SPI bus, so no Linux driver
+		 * claims it: keep it on, or the trusted application cannot
+		 * initialise the sensor (errors 1043/1064).
+		 */
 		vreg_l1c_1p8: ldo1 {
 			regulator-name = "vreg_l1c_1p8";
 			regulator-min-microvolt = <1800000>;
 			regulator-max-microvolt = <1800000>;
 			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
+			regulator-boot-on;
+			regulator-always-on;
 		};
 
 		vreg_l2c_1p8: ldo2 {
-- 
